## Run

From this directory:

```bash
gmk run
```

`gmk run` reads `.gmkrc.json` and starts Compose watch, host Air, or `go run cmd/main.go`. Use `gmk run --dry-run` to print the command, `gmk run --host` to run the app on the host (Compose infra only), and `gmk run --detach` for `docker compose up -d --build` without file watch.

{{ if .WithDocker }}
Live reload (same as `gmk run` when Docker is available):

```bash
docker compose up --watch --build
```

Detached, no file watch:

```bash
docker compose up -d --build
```

Host-side Go instead of the Compose `app` container (`gmk run --host` does this): start only the dependency names that exist in `docker-compose.yml`, then:

```bash
{{ if .WithAir }}air{{ else }}go run cmd/main.go{{ end }}
```

`.env` uses `localhost` for host processes. Compose overrides those hosts to Docker DNS (`mysql`, `redis`, `nats`, …).
{{ else }}
```bash
{{ if .WithAir }}air{{ else }}go run cmd/main.go{{ end }}
```
{{ end }}
{{- if .HasAuth }}

If you enabled auth, write a Stripe-style key (`svc_test_…`) before calling protected routes:

```bash
gmk key:generate
```
{{- end }}

## Check it

{{ if eq .ProjectType "grpc" }}
gRPC listens on `{{.Port}}`. The scaffold includes `api/proto/health.proto` (`HealthService.Check`) and registers gRPC health + reflection. Compile new `.proto` files with `protoc` in your own workflow.
{{ else }}
```bash
curl http://localhost:{{.Port}}/healthz
curl http://localhost:{{.Port}}/readyz
```

API prefix comes from `API_ROUTE_VERSION` (default `/api/v1`). After `gmk make:service --name user`:

```bash
curl http://localhost:{{.Port}}/api/v1/users
```
